# Firebase Rules

- Use the project's established Firebase architecture.
- Use React Native Firebase when the project is configured with it.
- Do not initialize Firebase repeatedly.
- Keep Firebase configuration separate from UI components.
- Do not put Firebase implementation details directly inside screens.
- Encapsulate Firebase operations inside services/hooks.
- Use TypeScript types for Firebase data.
- Never hardcode secrets or credentials.
- Do not log authentication tokens or sensitive user data.
- Handle Firebase errors explicitly.
- Clean up Firebase listeners/subscriptions when necessary.
- Use Firestore queries efficiently.
- Avoid unnecessary real-time listeners.
- Follow the project's security rules and least-privilege principles.